<https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/assessment/morphoeval-delphi10000-anchiornis-huxleyi-turing-wavelength-s0-overall> a pk:LLMClaimAssessment ;
    rdfs:label "Anchiornis huxleyi Turing wavenumber at 2.0 nm (Late Jurassic, 160.0 Ma) — MorphoEval overall 89.0/100" ;
    dct:date "2026-10-27"^^xsd:date ;
    dct:description "Pass 2 of the 2.0 nm detail-scale Schnakenberg model (a=0.062, b=1.28, Du=0.72, Dv=31.5) at 160.0 Ma, chronoseries 1/1. Analytical lambda_c is 2.0 nm; the nonlinear band-weighted wavelength is 2.517 nm and is now archived in the reference JSON. Wide versus tight holotype ROIs differ by foreground delta -0.0082. The comparison figure draws the equal-diffusion control field (std 0.00231, sigma_max -0.447) beside the patterned field (std 0.367). Dispersion fit Pearson r=0.99999999, RMSE=6.1e-5. GIF is 12 frames at 640x480; last-frame CV similarity to the holotype is 96.0. Overall 89.0/100. The 29 nm envelope remains the coarser mode (ratio 14.45); there is no successor chronospecies. Overall 89.0/100 (faithfulness 88.4, reproducibility 90.2); rubric morphoeval 0.1.0; checkpoint commit 0c76d15d14afcec6c366e1b9274a6586a0de48fc; environment: . Dimension assessments: Model fidelity to source 91, Morphological realism / specimen match 86, Parameter expressivity 90, Morphometric validation 88, Source and data traceability 93, Code-to-model traceability 87, Reproducibility package 90. Output judged: docs/media/anchiornis_huxleyi_turing_wavelength_s0_comparison.png: rendered output of models/2026-delphi10000-anchiornis-huxleyi-turing-wavelength-s0.py at 0c76d15d14afcec6c366e1b9274a6586a0de48fc, image/png, 715328 B, 1512×984 px, artifact_sha256 03cc50852277a520c6034147c3fffb536bb7626b53f3c27776f3b7aa618be062 (sha256 03cc50852277a520c6034147c3fffb536bb7626b53f3c27776f3b7aa618be062), spec_fingerprint cfa4a6e3c12e35a065d167ae369156e69e22c3638b6152ea6a89f2120ac783ec. Dual provenance: spec_fingerprint: cfa4a6e3c12e35a065d167ae369156e69e22c3638b6152ea6a89f2120ac783ec; artifact_sha256: 03cc50852277a520c6034147c3fffb536bb7626b53f3c27776f3b7aa618be062; input_dataset_sha256: {datasets/anchiornis_huxleyi_turing_wavelength_s0/anchiornis_huxleyi_holotype.jpg=4415de64f740a3c5..., datasets/anchiornis_huxleyi_turing_wavelength_s0/anchiornis_huxleyi_turing_wavelength_s0_reference.json=48ac4e1877f3ba4b..., datasets/anchiornis_huxleyi_turing_wavelength_s0/paper_citations.bib=34ab76031ac68848...}. Supersedes audit: 2026-10-27-anchiornis-huxleyi-turing-wavelength-s0-audit. Claim boundary: reported_in_source: Xu et al. 2009: Anchiornis huxleyi holotype IVPP V14378, Tiaojishan Formation, pennaceous feathers on forelimbs and hindlimbs. | Li et al. 2010: melanosome shape is the evidence for Anchiornis plumage color. Organelle lengths are hundreds of nanometres. | Turing 1952: a critical wavenumber k_c when the inhibitor diffuses sufficiently faster than the activator. | Watt, Bothma and Meredith 2009: eumelanin is a stacked oligomeric sheet at nanometre scale.; reconstructed_in_script: Schnakenberg kinetics and the dispersion relation, with parameters chosen for this 2.0 nm detail slot. | Length unit that places analytical lambda_c at 2.0e-9 m. | Equal-diffusion ablation drawn as a field, Dv sweep, pure-mode growth-rate fit, and a second holotype ROI. | Final GIF frame: holotype photograph times a weak function of the simulated field.; transfer_boundary: 2.0 nm is the assigned detail scale identified with the melanin sheet mode. Li et al. 2010 did not measure 2.0 nm. | The museum photograph is not a 2 nm micrograph. Image fitness compares the registered final frame to that photograph.; does_not_claim: That Schnakenberg kinetics are the Anchiornis melanin pathway. | That a successor chronospecies of Anchiornis exists in this series. | That slot 1229 parameters were copied. That slot publishes none. | That these nanopublications were cryptographically signed. No nanopub profile was present.." ;
    dct:subject <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/concept/morphoeval-rubric-0.1.0> ;
    pk:assessedBy <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/model/grok-4.7> ;
    pk:assessmentType "morphoeval/0.1.0/overall" ;
    pk:evidenceAgainst "remediation needed: {'id': 'R1', 'item': 'RESOLVED in pass 2. Wide (18-82%) and tight (30-70%) holotype ROIs; foreground delta -0.0082.'}",
        "remediation needed: {'id': 'R2', 'item': 'RESOLVED in pass 2. The comparison figure draws the equal-diffusion control field, std 0.00231.'}",
        "remediation needed: {'id': 'R3', 'item': 'RESOLVED in pass 2. reference JSON measured_nonlinear_wavelength.band_weighted_wavelength_nm = 2.517 next to analytical 2.0 nm.'}" ;
    pk:hasScore 8.9e-01 ;
    pk:hasVerdict "faithful" .

